<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uí Chonaill Gabra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uí Chonaill Gabra were a branch of the Uí Fidgenti of early medieval Munster, holding territory in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-limerick">County Limerick</a>, where the barony of Connello preserves their name. Their kings, later known by the surname Ó Coileáin (Collins), lost their lands to Anglo-Norman settlers, especially the FitzGeralds, in the late 12th and 13th centuries and moved into west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a>.</p></div>
